</Data><Data name="lines"><value>South Watermill - East Watermill 765 kV Line; East Watermill 765 kV Switch; Watermill Switch – Stainback Switch 345kV Double-Circuit Line Upgrade; Loop Nine Switch - Watermill Switch 345 kV Line; Watermill Switch – Wilson Switch 138 kV Double-Circuit Line; Watermill to Reindeer 138 kV Line</value></Data><Data name="stages"><value>built 1; approved 3; planned 2</value></Data><Data name="builders"><value>ONCOR</value></Data><Data name="location_quality"><value>exact</value></Data><Data name="location_basis"><value>GIS check Oct 19, 2026: matched by name to 'WATERMILL' in the HIFLD Electric Substations layer (345 kV, in service); the earlier estimate was 0.21 mi away. Earlier note: PUC Docket 57918 order says Watermill switch is about 3.5 mi west of the IH-45 / Malloy Bridge Rd intersection. The point is that intersection (OSM 32.5612, -96.6643) moved 3.5 mi west. It lands on Watermill Rd, which fits.</value></Data><Data name="market"><value>ERCOT (Texas)</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>-96.72618,32.55854,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Euclid</name><styleUrl>#sub-new</styleUrl><ExtendedData><Data name="feature_type"><value>substation</value></Data><Data name="id"><value>euclid-caldwell</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>Euclid</value></Data><Data name="county"><value>Caldwell</value></Data><Data name="status"><value>new</value></Data><Data name="there_now"><value>no</value></Data><Data name="work"><value>building a new substation</value></Data><Data name="work_stage"><value>approved</value></Data><Data name="work_in_service"><value>2026-11</value></Data><Data name="work_project"><value>Euclid_Substation_Addition_Updated</value></Data><Data name="status_reason"><value>ERCOT's project describes it as new</value></Data><Data name="max_kv"><value>765</value></Data><Data name="next_in_service"><value>2026-11</value></Data><Data name="queue_projects"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="queue_mw"><value