e></Data><Data name="market"><value>ERCOT (Texas)</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>-100.1895,35.2723,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CTT Cross Substation</name><styleUrl>#sub-unconfirmed</styleUrl><ExtendedData><Data name="feature_type"><value>substation</value></Data><Data name="id"><value>ctt-cross-substation-hall</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>CTT Cross Substation</value></Data><Data name="county"><value>Hall</value></Data><Data name="status"><value>unconfirmed</value></Data><Data name="there_now"><value>unknown</value></Data><Data name="work"><value>new line or substation work planned</value></Data><Data name="work_stage"><value>proposed</value></Data><Data name="work_in_service"><value>2031</value></Data><Data name="work_project"><value>Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan</value></Data><Data name="status_reason"><value>not on public maps by this name, and ERCOT doesn't say it is new; could be new or renamed</value></Data><Data name="max_kv"><value>345</value></Data><Data name="next_in_service"><value>2031</value></Data><Data name="queue_projects"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="queue_mw"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="check_link"><value>https://www.google.com/maps/@?api=1&amp;map_action=map&amp;center=34.39390,-100.89410&amp;zoom=16&amp;basemap=satellite</value></Data><Data name="line_count"><value>1</value></Data><Data name="lines"><value>Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan</value></Data><Data name="stages"><value>proposed 1</value></Data><Data name="builders"><value>Cross Texas and AEP</value></Data><Data name="location_quality"><value>town</value></Data><Data name="location_basis"><value>Placed at the town of Turkey: CTT labels this load site 'Cross/Turkey', and the georeferenced Option 1 map puts Cross near Turkey (about 10 mi uncertainty). Cross is on CTT's Silverton-Tesla 345 kV line, so Briscoe or Motley County cannot be ruled out.</value></Data><Data name="market"><value>ERCOT (Texas)</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>-100.8941,34.3939,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>CTT Gray Substation</name><styleUrl>#sub-unconfirmed</styleUrl><ExtendedData><Data name="feature_type"><value>substation</value></Data><Data name="id"><value>ctt-gray-substation-gray</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>CTT Gray Substation</value></Data><Data name="county"><value>Gray</value></Data><Data name="status"><value>unconfirmed</value></Data><Data name="there_now"><value>unknown</value></Data><Data name="work"><value>new line or substation work planned</value></Data><Data name="work_stage"><value>proposed</value></Data><Data name="work_in_service"><value>2028-04</value></Data><Data name="work_project"><value>New CTT Celtic Green 345 kV station</value></Data><Data name="status_reason"><value>not on public maps by this name, and ERCOT doesn't say it is new; could be new or renamed</value></Data><Data name="max_kv"><value>345</value></Data><Data name="next_in_service"><value>2028-04</value></Data><Data name="queue_projects"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="queue_mw"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="check_link"><value>https://www.google.com/maps/@?api=1&amp;map_action=map&amp;center=35.40751,-100.81984&amp;zoom=16&amp;basemap=satellite</value></Data><Data name="line_count"><value>2</value></Data><Data name="lines"><value>Panhandle Reliability Transmission Plan; New CTT Celtic Green 345 kV station</value></Data><Data name="stages"><value>proposed 2</value></Data><Data name="builders"><value>CTT; Cross Texas and AEP</value></Data><Data name="location_quality"><value>exact</value></Data><Data name="location_basis"><value>GIS check Oct 19, 2026: matched by name to 'GRAY' in the HIFLD Electric Substations layer (345 kV, in service); the earlier estimate was 1.68 mi away. Earlier note: PUC Docket 37956 says Gray Substation is about 2 mi west-southwest of Lefors. The point is Lefors (OSM 35.4385, -100.8040) moved 2 mi WSW.</value></Data><Data name="market"><value>ERCOT (Texas)</value></Data></ExtendedData><Point><coordinates>-100.81984,35.40751,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Celtic Green</name><styleUrl>#sub-unconfirmed</styleUrl><ExtendedData><Data name="feature_type"><value>substation</value></Data><Data name="id"><value>celtic-green-wheeler</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>Celtic Green</value></Data><Data name="county"><value>Wheeler</value></Data><Data name="status"><value>unconfirmed</value></Data><Data name="there_now"><value>unknown</value></Data><Data name="work"><value>new line or substation work planned</value></Data><Data name="work_stage"><value>proposed</value></Data><Data name="work_in_service"><value>2028-07</value></Data><Data name="work_project"><value>New double circuit line from CTT Railhead to Celtic Green</value></Data><Data name="status_reason"><value>not on public maps by this name, and ERCOT doesn't say it is new; could be new or renamed</value></Data><Data name="max_kv"><value>345</value></Data><Data name="next_in_service"><value>2028-07</value></Data><Data name="queue_projects"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="queue_mw"><value>0</value></Data><Data name="check_link"><value>https://www.google.com/maps/@?api=1&amp;map_action=map&amp;center=35.21594,-100.28101&amp;zoom=16&amp;basemap=satellite</value></Data><Data name="line_count"><value>1</value></Data><Data name="lines"><value>New double circuit line from CTT Railhead to Celtic Green</value></Data><Data name="stages"><value>proposed 1</value></Data><Data name="builders"><value>CTT</value></Data><Data name="location_quality"><value>approx</value></Data><Data name="location_basis"><value>ERCOT: CTT's new Celtic Green 765/345 kV substation cuts into the existing Gray-Tesla 345 kV double-circuit line about 39 mi from Gray. Placed 39 mi along the OSM geometry of that line (LS Power way 453794445) from Gray. The error could pass 2 mi if ERCOT's 39 mi is a straight-line figure.</value></Data><Data name="market"><value>E